            <ArticleTitle>Atypical odontalgia. A report of twenty-two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The findings in twenty-two cases of a condition that causes pain in the teeth and gingivae are presented. Two cases are described in detail. The importance of recognizing the problem and avoiding unnecessary dental treatment is stressed. The most effective treatment appears to be reassurance and the use of antidepressant drugs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
